          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I have stage 3 kidney disease and high blood pressure. Does the classification link the two, and what target does guidance describe for someone like me?",
          "answer": "You should seek medical attention regarding your stage 3 kidney disease and high blood pressure. \n\n[removed: this system does not give doses or amounts.] Both conditions—chronic kidney disease and hypertension—are interconnected, as high blood pressure can further impair kidney function, and kidney disease can elevate blood pressure (source: \"Hypertension and Chronic Conditions\"). \n\nFor someone in your situation, guidelines generally recommend a target blood pressure of less than 130/80 mm Hg (source: “Coronary artery disease: secondary prevention after a diagnosis,” “Hypertension: when treatment starts and which options are first-line”). It is important to engage in lifestyle modifications, including dietary changes, physical activity, and weight management, alongside monitoring your health regularly with your healthcare provider (source: \"Hypertension and Lifestyle Changes\"). Always discuss specific goals and treatment options with your clinician for personalized medical advice.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
